Mean modulus ≈ 257 bar, mean pore fraction ≈ 0.472. High run-to-run variability. Runs 5 and 6 show high modulus (~324–330) but low pore fraction (~0.384–0.390). Runs 3–4 show lower modulus but higher pore fraction. No consistent Pareto-dominant point.

**The 17-0add-15deg-200s-N2-1800s_run2** (mixing_temp=25, bath_temp=15, pullcast_speed=15, wait=200s, nips=1800s): Modulus=373, PF=0.362 — single run, high modulus but low pore fraction.

