## Step 3: Identify Promising Unexplored Region

The data suggests:
- Higher bath_temp (15–22°C) with polymer_wt=17 tends to give moderate-to-high modulus
- Longer wait times (200–600s) with bath_temp=5 give high modulus but lower pore fraction
- The combination of **moderate bath_temp (~15–19°C)** with **moderate wait time** and **polymer_wt=17** appears promising for balanced performance

Looking at the best single-run observations for joint performance:
