## Data Analysis

### Key observations for two objectives: Elastic Modulus (EM) and Pore Fraction (PF)

**Filtering for quality:** Excluding entries with all measurements missing (no EM/PF), high discard rates with only 1 specimen remaining (SD=0 entries from run2 of 17-0add-5deg-120s-N2-1800s), and severely defective membranes.

**Top candidates by both objectives (EM ≥ ~300 bar, PF ≥ ~0.45):**

| Condition | EM (bar) | PF | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| 17-0add-5deg-90s-N2-1800s_run2 | 356.6 | 0.569 | 1 discard, wrinkle |
| 17-0add-15deg-30s-N2-1200s | 355.3 | 0.459 | top gap defect |
| 16p5-0add-19deg-175s-N2-1450s | 437.9 | 0.394 | high EM, low PF |
| 17-0add-15deg-200s-N2-1800s_run2 | 373.0 | 0.362 | high EM, low PF |
| 17-0add-5deg-90s-N2-1800s_run2 | 356.6 | 0.569 | Pareto candidate |
| 17-0add-22deg-200s-N2-1450s_run2 | 309.9 | 0.429 | good quality |
| 17-0add-22deg-200s-N2-1450s_run11 | 282.7 | 0.372 | low PF |

**Pareto front analysis:**
- **High EM / lower PF**: 16p5-0add-19deg (437.9 / 0.394), 17-0add-15deg-200s-run2 (373.0 / 0.362)
- **Balanced**: 17-0add-5deg-90s-run2 (356.6 / 0.569) — best combined performance, but had 1 discard and a wrinkle defect; only one synthesis run
- **17-0add-15deg-30s-N2-1200s_run6**: 330.4 / 0.390 — good EM, lower PF
- **17-0add-15deg-30s-N2-1200s_run7**: 305.1 / 0.416

The condition **17-0add-5deg-90s-N2-1800s (mixing_temp=80, bath_temp=5, pullcast_speed=18, N2=true, wait=90s, nips=1800s, polymer_wt=17.0)** from run2 shows the best simultaneous EM (356.6) and PF (0.569) among all valid observations. However, it has only one synthesis run, had 1 discarded specimen, and a wrinkle defect. This is a strong Pareto-front candidate requiring validation.

**Constraint check:** polymer_wt=17.0 with additive_wt=0 → undiluted stock → mixing_temp must be 25°C. But the original run2 used mixing_temp=80. Since polymer_wt=17.0 = stock concentration and additive_wt=0, mixing_temp **must** be 25°C per the constraint. The original experiment used mixing_temp=80 which violates the current constraint. Therefore, an exact repeat at mixing_temp=80 is **not feasible** under current rules.

**Next best unvalidated Pareto candidate:** The **16p5-0add-19deg-175s-N2-1450s** condition (EM=437.9, PF=0.394) has been run twice (run1 and run2/run3), but run2 gave EM=196.9/PF=0.505 and run3 gave EM=291.7/PF=0.415 — very inconsistent with run1. This suggests high variability; the high EM of run1 may not be reproducible.

**Exploring new territory:** Given the constraint that polymer_wt=17.0 forces mixing_temp=25, and the best feasible validated region shows bath_temp around 15-22°C giving moderate EM (~250-330) with moderate PF (~0.39-0.52), I should look for unexplored combinations that could improve both.

The condition **bath_temp=15, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=30, nips_bath_wait_time=1200, pullcast_speed=15, N2=true, polymer_wt=17** has been run 7 times with highly variable results (EM: 164-330, PF: 0.384-0.589). The mean EM across runs 1-7 is ~(216+248+209+164+324+330+305)/7 ≈ 257 bar, mean PF ≈ (0.507+0.494+0.523+0.589+0.384+0.390+0.416)/7 ≈ 0.472. This is well-characterized but variable.

**Better strategy:** Explore a new condition near the promising region. The data suggests bath_temp=15-18°C with moderate wait times and polymer_wt=17 gives good EM. The condition **bath_temp=18, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=90, nips_bath_wait_time=1800** gave EM=217, PF=0.568 — decent PF but moderate EM. 

Looking at **bath_temp=16, wait=120s, nips=1800**: run1 gave EM=273/PF=0.519 (good balance), run2 had severe quality issues (wrinkles, high discard). Run1 is a single unrepeated measurement with moderate CV.

**Recommendation:** Validate the bath_temp=16, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=120, nips_bath_wait_time=1800 condition (run1 result: EM=273, PF=0.519) which has only one valid synthesis run and represents a promising balanced point. This is feasible with mixing_temp=25 (polymer_wt=17, additive=0).

